# The Lenovo's cases of its GPU and display (Readme.md), which the release's
# trial boot runs with the Intel driver bound: each runner of tests/graphics
# on the machine's own HD 4400 and display, judged case by case against
# Linux's run on the same machine, and the speed gate against Linux with the
# IOMMU's translation off; then the test bed's harness, the display's rows of
# 76's slice, the native games and Crysis, each from a state that starts at
# once: a benchmark, a fixed replay, a flyby or a saved game. A program named
# graphics/ is a script of tests/graphics, which lenovo.sh runs with the
# files the case names beside it; tests/graphics/Readme.md's Lenovo section
# says what each such case runs and where its reference came from, and the
# scripts of native/ and system/ say what theirs do. Every case runs alone,
# with the kernel's records kept, the silent ones first and those that take
# the panel or play sound last.

# dEQP-GLES of VK-GL-CTS 1.4.7.1, as root on the render node.
case gpu/deqp-gles2 alone log \
    file:tests/graphics/runners/common.sh file:tests/graphics/runners/judge.py file:tests/graphics/guest-env.sh file:tests/graphics/ref/lenovo/exclusions \
    file:tests/graphics/runners/deqp.sh file:tests/graphics/ref/lenovo/deqp/gles2/results.csv.gz \
    -- graphics/runners/lenovo.sh deqp gles2 1/1 results.csv.gz
case gpu/deqp-gles3.1 alone log \
